 value (RFC 8259): `undefined`, `NaN`/`Infinity`, `Date`, `Map`, `bigint`, functions, symbol keys or sparse arrays.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the merged document as a new value;
+neither argument is mutated. An object patch is merged recursively into the target (into `{}` if the target is not
+an object): a `null` member removes that member, other values add or replace it. Any non-object patch (including
+arrays and `null`) replaces the target, so arrays are replaced, never merged, and a merge patch cannot set a value
+to `null`. It throws `JsonMergePatchError` if the target or the patch is not a JSON value (RFC 8259). RFC 7396
+obsoletes RFC 7386 with the same algorithm.
